<section class="section process" data-cms-section="process" data-cms-section-name="Process"><div class="process-copy cms-process-wide"><p class="section-label" data-cms-editable>04 / From exposure to positive</p><h2 data-cms-editable>The parameters are read in relation to the result, not memorized as a fixed recipe.</h2><div class="process-list"><article class="process-item"><span>01</span><h3 data-cms-editable>Exposure</h3><p data-cms-editable>Metering, working EI, tonal placement, reciprocity and the particular limits of X-ray film.</p></article><article class="process-item"><span>02</span><h3 data-cms-editable>First development</h3><p data-cms-editable>Time, temperature, agitation, developer and dilution as variables that change the final positive.</p></article><article class="process-item"><span>03</span><h3 data-cms-editable>Reversal</h3><p data-cms-editable>Bleaching, clearing, re-exposure and second development treated as one connected chain.</p></article><article class="process-item"><span>04</span><h3 data-cms-editable>Reading the result</h3><p data-cms-editable>Shadows, midtones, highlights and defects used to decide what the next test should change.</p></article></div></div></section>
